{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-sg0","title":"Plan: replace bd with kb-native issue tracker (drop dolt)","design":"# PLAN: Replace beads (bd) with a kb-native issue tracker (drop dolt)\n\n## Motivation\n\nbd works conceptually (DAG deps, epics, ready/blocked, the review/dispatch\nworkflows) but the dolt backend is an operational tax — this session alone:\nbreaker false-open under load, migration wedge on dirty working sets, a 0.60→1.0\nschema upgrade, and a 6-database migration. bd is also far larger than we use\n(60+ commands: wisps, molecules, swarms, gates, federation, merge-slots,\ncompaction). And the kb-7g9.5 \"ingest bd into kb\" approach DUPLICATES content\n(mirror of dolt in kb).\n\nGoal: make **kb the source of truth** for issues — issues live in kb's single\nSQLite DB (no server, no dolt), are vector+FTS searchable, and open AND closed\nissues are surfaced into agent context via the existing hooks. Keep the parts we\nvalue (DAG dependency tracking, epics/children, ready/blocked, the\nexpert-review/implementation-review/dispatch workflows). Drop dolt and bd's\ncomplexity. Supersedes kb-7g9.5 (ingest-mirror) and kb-7g9.6 (surfacing) and\nfolds in kb-k3i (domain-aware open-issue injection).\n\n## Investigation summary (verified against ../beads + kb sources)\n\nbd data model: issues(id, title, description, design, status, priority,\nissue_type, parent via hierarchical id, assignee, timestamps, close_reason,\nmetadata) + dependencies(issue_id, depends_on_id, type) + labels + comments +\nevents. DAG types that affect ready/blocked: `blocks`, `parent-child` (children\ninherit parent's blocked state), plus niche `conditional-blocks`/`waits-for`.\n`bd ready` = status in (open,in_progress) AND is_blocked=0 (denormalized,\nrecomputed by transitive closure); `bd blocked` = is_blocked=1 + active blockers.\nIDs: `\u003cprefix\u003e-\u003chash\u003e` roots + `\u003cparent\u003e.\u003cN\u003e` children (child_counters table).\n\ndolt coupling (the drop target): MySQL-protocol sql-server, branches, push/pull\nreplication, dolt history/compaction/flatten, the circuit breaker. ALL of\nready/blocked, dep traversal, label/comment/event logging is pure SQL that runs\nidentically on plain SQLite. The thin dolt layer is droppable.\n\nWorkflow contract (the ~18 ops the workflows actually use):\n- planning: `create --type=epic --design-file=PATH`; `create --type=task --parent=EPIC`\n- expert-review: `show EPIC` → read `.design` (file PATH, not content); rejects a\n  plan whose deferral references lack a bd-ID.\n- implementation-review: `show EPIC`, list children.\n- /dispatch: `show EPIC`; `list --status=open --parent=EPIC`; `update TASK --claim`\n  (ATOMIC, no double-claim); `close TASK`; `dep list EPIC` filtered to\n  `discovered-from`.\n- the discovered-from discipline: `create --deps=discovered-from:EPIC`; query it.\n- project-manager (read-only): list/blocked/stale/search/stats/children.\nEverything else bd exposes (wisps, molecules, gates, federation, dolt, compact)\nis UNUSED by our workflows → dropped.\n\nkb substrate (verified): SQLite + sqlite-vec + FTS5 at ~/.cache/kb/knowledge.db.\nThe EntityRepository pattern (kb/entities/) already adds typed entities with\ntheir own `\u003centity\u003e`, `\u003centity\u003e_vec`, `\u003centity\u003e_fts` tables + role-typed junction\ntables. ConceptRepository (kb/entities/concepts.py) is an exact template: status\nenum, project scope, add/get/list/search(vector), supersede, and\n`concept_theorems`/`concept_findings` role-typed edges == the dependency-edge\npattern. HybridSearch (vector+FTS+RRF) is reusable for issue search.\nopen_issues_surface.py currently shells `bd list --status=open --json`; switching\nit to a kb table is a localized change.\n\n## Architecture: kb-native tracker (\"kb issues\")\n\nSingle SQLite DB (kb's existing knowledge.db), WAL mode, no server. New kb entity:\n\n- `kb/entities/issues.py` → `IssuesRepository` (modeled on ConceptRepository).\n- Tables: `issues`, `issues_vec` (description embedding), `issues_fts`, `issue_deps`.\n- `issues` columns (the bd-essential subset, NOT the wisp/molecule/gate/federation\n  bloat): id, type (task|bug|feature|epic|chore|spike|decision), status\n  (open|in_progress|blocked|closed), priority (0-4), parent_id, title,\n  description, design_file (path), assignee, close_reason, project, tags(JSON),\n  created_at, updated_at, started_at, closed_at, closed_by_session.\n  (bd's extra statuses — defer/pin/hook — and defer-until scheduling are dropped,\n  unused.)\n- `issue_deps` columns: issue_id, depends_on_id, type\n  (blocks|parent-child|discovered-from|related|supersedes), created_at, created_by.\n  ready/blocked-affecting subset = {blocks, parent-child}.\n- ready/blocked: computed on-demand via recursive SQL (an issue is READY iff\n  status in (open,in_progress) AND no open `blocks`-blocker AND its parent (if\n  any) is not blocked). No denormalized is_blocked initially (hundreds of issues\n  → fast); add a materialized column later only if a query is slow.\n- ID scheme: KEEP bd's scheme for continuity — `\u003cprefix\u003e-\u003chex\u003e` roots +\n  `\u003cparent\u003e.\u003cN\u003e` children — so existing ids (kb-7g9, kb-7g9.5) and all\n  plan-file / discovered-from / kb-id references stay valid post-migration.\n\n## CLI: a bd-compatible shim (so workflows/hooks are UNCHANGED)\n\nWe do NOT reimplement bd's 60 commands — only the ~18-op contract. Provide:\n- `kb issue \u003cadd|show|list|update|close|dep|ready|blocked|search\u003e` (native).\n- a thin `bd`-compatible front that maps the contract subcommands\n  (`bd create/show/update --claim/close/list --status --parent/dep add/dep list/\n  ready/blocked/search`) onto `kb issue`, emitting the SAME `--json` shapes the\n  hooks/workflows parse. Installed AS `bd` (replacing the npm binary) so\n  CLAUDE.md, /dispatch, the review agents, and the surfacing hooks need no\n  command changes — only their backend changes.\n- Claim atomicity: `UPDATE issues SET status='in_progress', assignee=? WHERE id=?\n  AND status IN ('open','blocked')` → rowcount==1 means claimed (SQLite WAL,\n  single-host multi-process safe).\n\n## Surfacing (the user's core want)\n\n- `open_issues_surface.py`: query the kb `issues` table directly (no server);\n  ADD vector search (embed the prompt → issues_vec) instead of pure\n  token-overlap; surface OPEN and recently-CLOSED issues ([OPEN-ISSUE]/\n  [RESOLVED-ISSUE]) — closed issues are prior-art (\"this was already\n  done/decided\"). Folds in kb-k3i (domain-aware injection).\n- `compose_time_check.py`: add an [OPEN-ISSUE]/[RESOLVED-ISSUE] advisory class\n  from the issues table at compute-intent (Agent/Bash dispatch).\n- The embedding-down path already degrades to FTS (kb-zma) — issue surfacing\n  inherits it.\n\n## Migration (dolt → kb, one-time, fidelity-preserving)\n\nPer project DB (kb, am_rs, braidinfer, vllm, llamacpp, exterior_algebra):\n`bd export --json` (or direct SQL over the dolt server) → an importer that\ninserts into kb `issues` + `issue_deps`, PRESERVING ids, parent links, dep types,\nstatus (incl closed), design_file, timestamps. Closed issues imported too (prior\nart). Verify counts + a sample diff. THEN retire dolt + bd.\n\n## Workflow adaptation\n\nThe bd-shim means expert-review / implementation-review / /dispatch /\nthe discovered-from discipline / block-followup-without-bd-id run UNCHANGED (same\ncommands, kb backend). CLAUDE.md \"Planning and Review (Beads-Based)\" → reworded to\n\"kb-based\" (mechanical). project-manager's audit commands (stale/blocked/lint/\nfind-duplicates) map to kb issue queries; the niche ones it can lose.\n\n## What we DROP\n\ndolt entirely (server, branches, push/pull, history, compaction, breaker,\nmigrations); wisps/ephemeral, molecules/swarm/gates, federation/source_system,\nconditional-blocks/waits-for, merge-slot, the 40+ niche commands. If a dropped\nfeature is later needed, it is added to the kb tracker deliberately.\n\n## Phases (each a child task under the epic)\n\n1. IssuesRepository + schema (issues/_vec/_fts/issue_deps) + id scheme + CRUD +\n   vector/FTS search (clone ConceptRepository).\n2. ready/blocked recursive SQL + dep add/list + claim-atomic update.\n3. `kb issue` CLI + the `bd`-compatible shim (18-op contract, matching --json\n   shapes); ship behind a flag, validate against the live workflows.\n4. Migration importer (dolt export → kb issues, all 6 DBs, id/dep/status fidelity)\n   + a verification harness (counts + sample diff).\n5. Surfacing hooks: open_issues_surface + compose_time_check → kb issues, vector +\n   open/closed.\n6. Workflow/doc updates: CLAUDE.md \"Beads-Based\"→\"kb-based\"; confirm dispatch +\n   both review agents work on the shim.\n7. Cutover: switch `bd` to the shim, run the migration, retire dolt.service on\n   tardis + uninstall @beads/bd + archive .beads/. Tests green; one full\n   plan→review→dispatch→close loop on the new backend.\n\n## Risks / mitigations\n\n- Concurrency (multi-agent, one host): SQLite WAL + short transactions +\n  claim-via-UPDATE-rowcount. bd used dolt MVCC; WAL handles single-host\n  multi-process. (Multi-HOST sync — which dolt push/pull gave — is dropped; all\n  agents are on this host. If multi-host returns, revisit.)\n- ready/blocked perf: recursive SQL per `bd ready`; fine at our scale, materialize\n  later if needed.\n- Shim output fidelity: the hooks/workflows parse specific `--json` shapes; Phase\n  3 must reproduce them exactly (enumerate from the contract).\n- Migration fidelity: ids/deps/status must round-trip or plan-file/discovered-from\n  references break — verified by the Phase-4 harness before cutover.\n- Bootstrapping irony: this plan's epic is tracked in bd; it migrates into kb at\n  cutover.\n\n## Follow-ups (in bd)\n\n- kb-7g9.5: superseded by this epic (ingest-mirror replaced by source-of-truth); re-linked/closed when the epic is created.\n- kb-7g9.6 and kb-k3i: surfacing work folds into Phase 5 of this epic.\n","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-10T21:12:17Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T21:12:17Z","comments":[{"id":"019eb3ae-b17c-7acd-96dd-9ebb36818bb3","issue_id":"kb-sg0","author":"Bob McElrath","text":"EXPERT-REVIEW APPROVED (light/sonnet, comparative bd audit): keep/drop split validated, no over/under-ports; prior FULL-review 4 blockers all resolved (comments add, JSON-key mapping, surfacing project-isolation, child_counters); migration ordering correct; composability sound. One impl-note folded (Phase 8 which -a bd). Cleared to implement.","created_at":"2026-06-10T22:37:11Z"},{"id":"019eb5ed-ff8a-7efa-9bf1-464dcaa5f85f","issue_id":"kb-sg0","author":"Bob McElrath","text":"DESIGN DECISION (user): FULL RENAME bd-\u003ekbt, no bd command survives end-state. Reconciled with de-risking via a transition PASSTHROUGH inside kbt (shells to real bd while a project's backend flag is 'dolt'), so the bd-\u003ekbt rename is behaviorally a NO-OP until per-project flags flip. Rollout: build -\u003e rename(noop) -\u003e pilot(test proj) -\u003e incremental per-project opt-in -\u003e cutover deletes passthrough+bd+dolt. Plan updated (CLI/Surfacing/Workflow/Rollout/Phases 3,6,8). Surface change only; data model unchanged.","created_at":"2026-06-11T09:05:34Z"},{"id":"019eb5f2-1df1-7058-81bf-ff6b86829f0c","issue_id":"kb-sg0","author":"Bob McElrath","text":"LIGHT RE-REVIEW (kbt rename surface): APPROVED. No DESIGN-BLOCKING issues. Key implementation notes for Phase 3: (1) passthrough MUST use os.execvp (not subprocess.run) — only exec gives byte-identical stdin/stdout/stderr/exit-code/signal behavior for heredoc calls like 'bd comments add EPIC ... \u003c\u003cEOF'; subprocess silently breaks these. (2) backend flag precedence env-over-file must be stated explicitly in Phase 3 spec. (3) .beads/ walk-up detection for the flag must mirror bd's own cwd walk. (4) Phase 8 which -a bd misses shell functions/aliases — add 'type -a bd' check. All other passthrough edge cases (env forwarding, cwd preservation) are handled by os.execvp automatically. Rollout ordering is correct: passthrough in place (Ph3) → rename refs (Ph6, noop) → pilot → incremental opt-in → flip all flags → delete passthrough → remove bd. Coexistence correctness: dolt-flag projects unaffected; kb-flag projects interoperate correctly with global hooks (ID format unchanged, project-column isolation preserved).","created_at":"2026-06-11T09:10:04Z"},{"id":"019eb610-b767-7e66-a015-9dc531f1a0d2","issue_id":"kb-sg0","author":"Bob McElrath","text":"RE-REVIEW (light/sonnet, changed-surface) APPROVED, no design blockers. 4 Phase-3 impl-notes folded into plan: (1) passthrough=os.execvp not subprocess (byte-identical stdin/stdout/stderr/exit/signals); (2) flag precedence env KBT_BACKEND overrides .beads/config.yaml, test-only+logged; (3) .beads walk-up discovery not flat cwd check; (4) Phase 8 uses type -a bd not which -a bd (catches functions/aliases). Rollout ordering + coexistence confirmed correct; block-followup regex still matches (ID format preserved). Plan fully approved, dispatch-ready.","created_at":"2026-06-11T09:43:29Z"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":4}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-u76","title":"Fleet-wide bd upgrade from ../beads source (fixes circuit-breaker stale-open; installed=Mar-11)","description":"Installed @beads/bd is Mar-11; lacks circuitStaleTTL auto-reset -\u003e breaker stuck-open under load (kb-7g9.10). ../beads source (go1.26 builds) has the fix (circuitStaleTTL=5min, active-probe-on-cooldown, /tmp/beads-circuit subdir, CleanStaleCircuitBreakerFiles). Rebuild (go build ./cmd/bd) + replace ~/.nvm/.../node_modules/@beads/bd/bin/bd. COORDINATED: all agents share dolt at tardis:3308; a newer bd may migrate schema -\u003e upgrade ALL hosts together or verify schema-compat first. Interim mitigation live: bd-circuit-unstick.sh.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-10T13:55:59Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T14:24:30Z","closed_at":"2026-06-10T14:24:30Z","close_reason":"bd upgraded 0.60.0-\u003e1.0.5 (npm, this host's shared binary) + kb DB migrated to schema v49/metadata 1.0.5 (committed working set out-of-band, then bd migrate schema). Other project DBs migrate per-repo on first 1.0.5 use (broadcast sent).","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-u76","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9.10","type":"discovered-from","created_at":"2026-06-10T09:55:59Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.10","title":"P0 reliability: bd circuit-breaker must attempt auto-start on OPEN (self-defeating loop)","description":"Verified defect: when the dolt server dies, bd's circuit breaker trips OPEN and FAILS FAST, which BLOCKS the 'transparent auto-start' bd is supposed to do on demand -\u003e transient death becomes persistent outage needing manual bd dolt start. On open-breaker, attempt 'bd dolt start' before failing (or auto-start ahead of the breaker short-circuit). bd 0.60.0 here is behind 1.0.4 — check if fixed upstream; flag/upgrade.","notes":"RESOLVED (interim) via hook + ROOT CAUSE found in source. Installed bd = @beads/bd Mar-11 binary (~/.nvm/.../node_modules/@beads/bd/bin/bd): persists breaker in legacy /tmp/beads-dolt-circuit-3308.json and stays OPEN failing-fast indefinitely once tripped — it LACKS the stale-TTL auto-reset. The ../beads SOURCE (newer) already fixes this: circuit.go has circuitStaleTTL=5min (readState auto-resets open files older than 5min), active-probe-on-cooldown (open-\u003eclosed on reachable), CleanStaleCircuitBreakerFiles on init, and moved files to /tmp/beads-circuit/ subdir. INTERIM FIX (landed): hooks/misc/bd-circuit-unstick.sh (PreToolUse Bash) clears the stale-open legacy file when tardis:3308 is reachable, so bd re-probes immediately instead of failing-fast; leaves it intact when dolt is truly down. DURABLE FIX = rebuild+reinstall bd fleet-wide from ../beads (go1.26 available) -\u003e spun as follow-up (coordinated rollout; newer bd vs shared dolt schema risk). kb-7g9.9 (dolt CPUWeight/Restart) reduces the trigger.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:59:46Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T14:24:29Z","closed_at":"2026-06-10T14:24:29Z","close_reason":"Fixed by bd 1.0.5 upgrade (circuitStaleTTL auto-reset + active-probe + /tmp/beads-circuit subdir); interim unstick-hook removed; root cause was Mar-11 binary lacking stale-reset.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.10","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:59:46Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.9","title":"P0 reliability: supervise the shared dolt sql-server (systemd Restart=always)","description":"Root-caused this session: bd uses a SHARED dolt sql-server (127.0.0.1:3308, ~/.beads/shared-server/dolt) for all repos/agents; it died (no systemd unit supervises it) -\u003e total bd outage for every agent until manual 'bd dolt start'. Add a systemd --user unit (Restart=always) so server death auto-recovers. Single-point-of-failure for all bd ops; the whole surfacing system writes/reads bd.","notes":"DONE (2026-06-10): tardis ~/.config/systemd/user/dolt.service now Restart=always (was on-failure) + CPUWeight=10000 + IOWeight=1000 (applied live via systemctl --user set-property, no restart). Backup: dolt.service.bak-kb7g9-9. Goal: dolt wins CPU/IO under tardis contention (load ~13/20) so the bd breaker's query-probe doesn't time out and false-open. Effect: dolt select-1 latency 214ms-\u003e~180ms under load (marginal; dolt is a USER service so CPUWeight only prioritizes within user.slice, not vs system/other-user load). NOTE: this mitigates the TRIGGER but the FLAP root cause is kb-7g9.10 (breaker probe timeout too tight for under-load latency, not tunable -- Go binary). Will recur under heavy tardis load until breaker patched or load reduced.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:59:46Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T14:24:31Z","closed_at":"2026-06-10T14:24:31Z","close_reason":"dolt.service on tardis: Restart=always + CPUWeight=10000/IOWeight=1000 (live via set-property). Reduces breaker-trip trigger under load; pairs with the 1.0.5 breaker fix.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.9","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:59:45Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.1","title":"Multi-language kb ingest: Extractor seam + prune + content-addressed symbol identity","description":"Generalize ingest_python.py: factor a per-language Extractor (Python ast reused; Rust/C++/TS via tree-sitter; ctags fallback) feeding one embed/write pipeline. python_symbols-\u003ecode_symbols(+language). ADD PRUNE (re-ingest --files deletes symbols no longer in file; --deleted removes file's symbols) — fixes the stale-row 'lies about existing code' gap. Content-addressed symbol_id=hash(project,language,qualname) + content_hash for change/dedup. Physics extras (RETIRED_SYMBOLS/CANONICAL_FILES/frame_hint/notations) -\u003e per-project .claude/kb-ingest.json. Prereq for the code tiers.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:17:06Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T23:16:07Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T23:16:07Z","close_reason":"additive prune+content_hash landed + independently verified (temp-DB prune, empty-guard, hash); committed. code_symbols rename + multi-lang extractors remain (lockstep follow-on).","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.1","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:17:05Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.2","title":"Tier A: normalized-AST structural-hash function lineage (embedding-free, git-metadata-independent)","description":"Per function-version: structural_hash over normalized AST (alpha-rename own-name+locals, strip comments/format, KEEP calls+literals) -\u003e identity blind to name/path/position/cosmetic. Tracks fn through rename, file move, top/bottom move, delete-then-readd EXACTLY without git rename detection. Walk commit DAG (changed-files-per-commit); cluster versions into logical-function lineages (exact-hash edges); accumulate provenance timeline (names/paths/commits/status). No embedding server needed.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:17:06Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T23:21:50Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T23:21:50Z","close_reason":"Tier-A structural-hash + lineage landed; 20 invariant tests pass (rename/move/local-rename=same; return-type/decorator/logic=different; delete-readd+rename-move=same lineage); footprint clean; committed.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.2","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:17:05Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.3","title":"Tier C: sub-function shingle + MinHash/LSH containment (inline/extract + fragment reuse, embedding-free)","description":"Decompose each fn-version into normalized AST statement-shingles (k-gram + order-insensitive set); MinHash signature + LSH index. CONTAINMENT (asymmetric) surfaces extract (helper shingles subset original) and inline (fragment inside bigger fn) regardless of boundary/git. IDF/document-frequency down-weights boilerplate (self-suppresses ubiquitous patterns). Answers 'this fragment existed' where whole-fn vector NN is too coarse. Embedding-free (hashing+LSH); ash-outage-immune.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:17:06Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T23:24:25Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T23:24:25Z","close_reason":"Tier-C shingle+MinHash+containment landed; 12 tests pass; containment confirmed asymmetric |A∩B|/|A| (not Jaccard); extract/inline/IDF demonstrated; committed.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.3","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:17:06Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9","title":"Semantic prior-art surfacing — stop blind reimplementation (kb + bd + code; 3-tier lineage)","description":"Pre-emptive surfacing of prior art at act-time (PreToolUse Edit/Write/Task + UserPromptSubmit + Stop) so agents see existing findings, bd issues, and CODE before reimplementing. Engine exists (kb search = semantic over findings). Needs: multi-language code ingest (Extractor seam + prune + content-addressed identity), bd-\u003ekb ingest, and a 3-tier function-version model — A: normalized-AST structural hash (exact lineage through rename/move/delete-readd, embedding-free); C: shingle+MinHash/LSH containment (inline/extract + fragment reuse, embedding-free, IDF-weighted); B: embeddings (semantic rewrite, ash-gated). Current + history corpora, git-metadata-independent (distrust git rename detection). Function-first surfacing, file-as-metadata, LSP-composing. Plan: ~/.claude/plans/PLAN-semantic-prior-art-surfacing.md. Folds in kb-5ms, kb-mrl, kb-7lp, kb-k3i, kb-zma. ash:8081 currently down (mes reload) — Tier-B pieces gated on live test.","design":"# PLAN: Semantic prior-art surfacing — stop blind reimplementation\n\nEpic: kb-7g9\nGoal: at the moment an agent is about to act (write code, dispatch, edit), pre-emptively surface\nexisting **kb findings, bd issues, and CODE** that already do what it's about to do — so it stops\nreimplementing / re-deriving / contradicting prior work. The user's stated failure mode: \"I've\nutterly failed to get Claude to do pre-emptive research before blindly trudging into the side of a\nmountain; these hooks are the fix.\"\n\n## Files read in full (research, this plan)\n- `~/Projects/ai/kb/scripts/ingest_python.py` (the code-ingest path to generalize)\n- `~/Projects/ai/kb/kb/facade.py` `add_python_symbol` (embed-on-add: `embed_text = \"module.name: signature docstring\"`)\n- `~/Projects/ai/kb/kb_mcp_core.py` `kb_search` (semantic similarity over findings via `kb.search`)\n- `~/Projects/ai/kb/kb/core/embedding.py` (llama.cpp `/embedding` endpoint, token-embeddings mean-pooled, 4096-dim)\n- `~/Projects/ai/kb/scripts/hooks/post-commit-secular.sh` (current re-ingest trigger)\n- DB schema via sqlite (`findings`/`lean_theorems` populated + `_vec`; `python_symbols`/`scripts`/`concepts` empty; **no bd table**)\n\n## Verified substrate (what exists / what's missing)\n- **`kb search` is semantic** today (embed query → `findings_vec` sqlite-vec → similarity). Engine works; the surfacing hooks just token-match instead of calling it.\n- Per-corpus `_vec` + per-entity search is the existing architecture (`findings`/`lean_theorems`/`scripts`/`concepts`/`theorems`).\n- `add_python_symbol` **already embeds** per-symbol (`module.name: signature docstring`) — downstream is language-neutral.\n- **Gaps:** ingest is **commit-only, add-only, NO PRUNE** (deleted/renamed symbols leave stale rows → would surface non-existent code). Git hooks are sparse (only `claude` has post-commit; no post-merge/checkout/rewrite; target repos have none). **bd is not in the kb** (cannot be vector-searched). Code corpora (`python_symbols`/`scripts`) are empty.\n- **ash:8081 embedding server is currently down** (mes-researcher amdgpu reload) → the embedding-down STOP gate (kb-zma) is load-bearing; semantic surfacing must hard-STOP / FTS-fallback, never silently return empty.\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Corpus expansion (prerequisite)\n- **kb-7g9.1 — multi-language `kb ingest`:** factor a per-language **Extractor** (Python `ast` reused; Rust/C++/TS via **tree-sitter**; **ctags** fallback) feeding one embed/write pipeline. `python_symbols`→`code_symbols` (+`language`). **Add PRUNE** (`--files X` deletes vanished symbols; `--deleted F`). Content-addressed `symbol_id = hash(project,language,qualname)` + `content_hash`. Physics extras (`RETIRED_SYMBOLS`/`CANONICAL_FILES`/`frame_hint`/notations) → per-project `.claude/kb-ingest.json`.\n- **kb-7g9.5 — bd→kb ingest:** embed bd `title+description+design` into a `bd_issues` corpus (+`_vec`), synced on `bd create/update/close` (pattern: `bd_close_reingest.py`) + periodic resync. (Answers the user's explicit question: **yes**, bd must be embedded to vector-search it.)\n\n### Three identity/lineage tiers over function-versions (the hard-cases solution)\nDistrust git rename/path metadata entirely; re-derive identity from CONTENT over the commit DAG.\n- **kb-7g9.2 — Tier A: normalized-AST structural hash** (embedding-free). Alpha-rename own-name+locals, strip comments/format, KEEP calls+literals → hash blind to name/path/position/cosmetic. Tracks a function exactly through **rename, file move, top↔bottom move, delete-then-readd** with no git rename detection. Cluster versions into logical-function lineages; accumulate provenance timeline (names/paths/commits/status).\n- **kb-7g9.3 — Tier C: sub-function shingle + MinHash/LSH containment** (embedding-free). Normalized AST statement-shingles (k-gram + order-insensitive set) → MinHash signature → LSH index. **Asymmetric containment** surfaces **extract** (helper ⊆ original) and **inline** (fragment inside bigger fn) regardless of boundary or git hygiene. **IDF/document-frequency** down-weights boilerplate (ubiquitous patterns self-suppress). This is the answer to \"vector search isn't fuzzy\" — whole-function NN is too coarse for boundary-unstable refactors; containment over fragments is the right tool.\n- **kb-7g9.4 — Tier B: function/block embeddings** (ash-gated). Embed `qualname:signature:docstring` (+ block-level for migrated subspans) for \"different code, same intent\" (catches syntactic rewrites that A/C miss). **Current tier** (working tree, mutable, pruned to HEAD/branch) + **History tier** (deleted/reverted/branch-tip versions, content-deduped, provenance-tagged). Gated on ash + the embedding-down STOP.\n\nTiers compose: A=exact whole-fn, C=fragment/inline-extract, B=semantic rewrite. A and C are **embedding-free and ash-outage-immune** — the hardest cases (rename/move/delete-readd, inline/extract) are the cheap deterministic part; only B needs ash.\n\n### Surfacing (kb-7g9.6)\n- **`kb surface \"\u003ctext\u003e\" --sources findings,bd,code --limit 3`** — embed once, query `findings_vec` + `bd_vec` + code tiers (B cosine + C containment + A exact), merge.\n- Hook on **UserPromptSubmit + PreToolUse(Edit|Write|Task) + Stop** (the act-moments; PreToolUse Edit/Write is the \"walking into the mountain\" point).\n- **Function-first, file-as-metadata, LSP-composing:** output `qualname(sig) — \"docstring\" [module]`; file:line is metadata for the LSP jump. Index = semantic discovery; LSP = precise navigation. Agents see *functions*, not files.\n- **Layered triggers** (cheapest-first): (1) WRONG→RIGHT anti-pattern docs in the project persona/API.md; (2) project `reinvention-guard` pattern→symbol map (deterministic, catches trivial inline-math reinvention embeddings miss); (3) semantic + containment surface.\n- Reliability: `_seen` dedup (`code:\u003csymbol_id\u003e`), suppress-surface allowlist (e.g. \"assume Transformers attention works\"), embedding-down STOP (kb-zma).\n\n## Phases\n- **P1 (no ash):** kb-7g9.1 ingest generalization + PRUNE + content-id; kb-7g9.2 Tier-A structural-hash lineage. Anti-pattern docs + reinvention-guard (kb-7g9.6 layers 1–2). Immediate value, embedding-free.\n- **P2 (no ash):** kb-7g9.3 Tier-C shingle/containment + IDF. Full git triggers (post-commit/merge/checkout/rewrite) → current-tier always-fresh + prune.\n- **P3 (ash):** kb-7g9.4 Tier-B embeddings + current/history corpora; `kb surface` multi-source + the Edit/Write semantic surface hook. **LIVE-TEST gated** (kb-7g9.7).\n- **P4:** kb-7g9.5 bd→kb ingest + `--sources bd`; kb-k3i domain-aware injection; kb-mrl/kb-7lp semantic kb-context/UserPromptSubmit.\n\n## Live-test gates (on ash:8081 return — mes-researcher reloading)\nkb-7g9.7: confirm ash GGUF is **code-capable** (vs prose); calibrate similarity/containment thresholds, structural-hash normalization aggressiveness (over-collapse vs under-link), shingle k + min-fragment + IDF cutoff. Validate against the 3 measured exterior_algebra duplications (audie #5087) + the import-stat discoverability method (audie).\n\n## Follow-ups (in bd)\n- kb-7g9.1: multi-language ingest + prune + content-id (prerequisite).\n- kb-7g9.2: Tier-A structural-hash lineage.\n- kb-7g9.3: Tier-C shingle/MinHash/LSH containment + IDF.\n- kb-7g9.4: Tier-B embeddings + current/history corpora.\n- kb-7g9.5: bd→kb ingest.\n- kb-7g9.6: kb surface CLI + function-first/LSP surfacing + layered Edit/Write triggers.\n- kb-7g9.7: prereqs/calibration (ash code-model live check, AST-normalizer, granularity tuning).\n- kb-5ms: code/library-API semantic index (subsumed by kb-7g9.1+.4+.6 — close as dup or keep as the umbrella).\n- kb-mrl: kb-context.sh semantic injection (P4).\n- kb-7lp: UserPromptSubmit semantic kb query (P4).\n- kb-k3i: open_issues_surface domain-aware bd injection (P4).\n- kb-zma: embedding-down detection/STOP gate (cross-cutting reliability; required by Tier B + kb surface).\n\n## Notation\n- \"function-version\" = one (function, commit) content state; identity is content-addressed, not name/path.\n- Tiers: A=structural-hash (exact), C=shingle/containment (fragment), B=embedding (semantic).\n- \"current tier\" = working-tree state; \"history tier\" = deleted/reverted/other-branch versions.\n","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:16:30Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T10:03:15Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-5ms","title":"Code/library-API semantic index — surface existing implementations at Edit/Write time (the duplication fix)","description":"audie audit #5087: measured CODE duplication — 3 exterior_algebra scripts reinvented core.decomposition.decompose_hidden_states() AFTER it existed; agents find model/ (527 imports) but miss core/(222)/evaluation/(27)/data/(21). The kb-findings semantic surface (kb-mrl/7lp) covers PAST-EXPERIMENT entries, NOT the library API. To stop code reimplementation we must embed the library API (function sig+docstring per module) into a code index (python_symbols_vec/scripts_vec or code_chunks) and semantic-query it on PreToolUse Edit/Write/Task. This is the load-bearing piece of the prior-art-surfacing system for the 'walking into the mountain' problem. Complements: (a) per-project persona 'library-first checklist' naming commonly-missed submodules; (b) a Stop-hook promotion gate (new reusable fn in scripts/ -\u003e promote to library).","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T20:38:38Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T21:42:42Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T21:42:42Z","close_reason":"subsumed by kb-7g9 children (.1 ingest + .4 embeddings + .6 surface) per expert-review; tracked under the epic","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-mrl","title":"kb-context.sh: semantic-query injection, not recent-ids (user expects vector-query surfacing)","description":"audie audit (bridge #5073): kb-context.sh injects the 3 most-RECENT kb ids by project (recency, not relevance). User BELIEVES semantic injection happens (vector-query the conversation -\u003e surface relevant entries e.g. 9xe). It does not. Fix: kb-context.sh should run 'kb search \u003cfirst-prompt-snippet\u003e --project \u003cP\u003e --limit 5' to vector-query. Hybrid-workspace projects (exterior_algebra) get wrong-domain noise (kernel entries for a transformer-research session) under the recency window. High-value correctness/expectation gap.","notes":"(see code-index bd) audie #5089 git-archaeology REFUTES copy-hypothesis: the 3 dup scripts are INDEPENDENT re-derivations of ~2-line math (alpha=h@v1; h_perp=h-outer(alpha,v1)), not template copies. Library-first rule was present + function findable; agents inlined trivial math without looking. DESIGN REFINEMENT for the code index: pure name/signature embedding similarity may MISS trivial inline-math reinvention. Add (a) project-configurable REINVENTION-GUARD: pattern-\u003esymbol map (ast-grep/literal: 'alpha = h @ v1','h_perp = h -','def extract_v1','h[0]/h[0].norm()' -\u003e decompose_hidden_states/extract_v1) checked at PreToolUse Edit/Write on the about-to-be-written content; (b) WRONG-\u003eRIGHT anti-pattern examples in project API.md/persona ('if you write X, use Y') — strongest deterrent for simple-math reinvention. Semantic index catches concept similarity; pattern-guard catches known shapes deterministically; anti-pattern docs are the cheap immediate fix.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T20:19:10Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T20:55:34Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-bp4.6","title":"P7: port persona mechanism to global + de-physics bridge hooks (DONE)","description":"global session-persona.sh (generic, no case-map, git-root discovery) wired into global SessionStart; generic /persona command; de-physics'd bridge-resume/bridge-recv-prompt/session-start-resume/auto-resume (dropped persona-\u003ehandle map + ~/Physics/.persona paths + archie-KB block). Removed per-repo session-persona wiring + deleted stale copies in secular+claude. Commits: ~/.claude (session-persona+command+settings+4 hooks, 50cee85); secular; claude. Smoke-tested resolver (tip-mathlib-\u003etip). Acceptance scan: hooks/persona CLEAN of ~/Physics; residual = access-grants + skills (follow-ups created).","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:27:27Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T17:27:27Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T17:27:27Z","close_reason":"persona ported global, bridge hooks de-physics'd, committed 3 repos","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-bp4.6","depends_on_id":"kb-bp4","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T13:27:27Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-bp4.3","title":"P2/P3: de-physics global settings + provision per-repo (DONE)","description":"global 6f4533e (strip 16 entries + rm 7 files); secular 711bb2e (adopt 7 hooks canonical + wire 5 shared + bd_close_reingest + retarget Stop refs); claude 00910c1f (ref via secular abs path, drop cl44 check_symbols, add SubagentStop). Verified: global has zero physics-hook refs, generic surfacing kept, relocated hook fires. mathlib4 intentionally gets no .claude.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T16:32:42Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T16:32:42Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T16:32:42Z","close_reason":"committed across 3 repos; verified","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-bp4.3","depends_on_id":"kb-bp4","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T12:32:41Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-bp4.1","title":"P1a: wire guard-destructive-git + git-commit-check (DONE, committed be12efd)","description":"guard-destructive-git added to global PreToolUse/Bash; git-commit-check fixed (stdin JSON, was stale CLAUDE_TOOL_INPUT no-op) + wired to PostToolUse/Bash. Smoke-tested: destructive=exit2, safe=exit0, commit-check warns. Committed ~/.claude be12efd.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T15:35:30Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T15:47:05Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T15:47:05Z","close_reason":"wired + smoke-tested + committed be12efd","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-bp4.1","depends_on_id":"kb-bp4","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T11:35:29Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-bp4","title":"Generalize \u0026 de-physics global Claude hooks; port persona mechanism to ~/.claude","description":"Strip physics/lean/tex coupling from the GLOBAL ~/.claude/settings.json + hooks; move topic-specific hooks to per-repo Physics .claude/settings.json (secular canonical, mathlib4 needs one); generalize the persona mechanism (session-persona.sh + /persona) into ~/.claude leaving the 5 physics persona bodies in secular-constraints; move generic kb-surfacing hooks into ~/.claude/hooks/; wire the missing guard-destructive-git.sh; delete verified-dead + deprecated files. Plan: ~/.claude/plans/PLAN-generalize-claude-hooks.md. Cross-refs: kb-7mk (check_symbols global variant), kb-6hn (hooks-over-instructions cadence).","design":"# PLAN: Generalize \u0026 de-physics the global Claude hook + persona system\n\nEpic: kb-bp4\nProject root (primary edits): `~/Projects/ai/claude` (= `~/.claude`); secondary: `~/Physics/{secular-constraints,claude,mathlib4}`, `~/Projects/ai/kb`.\n\n## Files read in full\n\nGlobal config + hooks (`~/.claude`):\n- `settings.json` (the wiring source-of-truth)\n- `hooks/session-init.sh`, `hooks/build-status.sh`, `hooks/history-isolation.sh`, `hooks/dedupe-file-reads.sh`\n- `hooks/lib/beads-plan.sh`, `lib/provider-context.sh`, `lib/ash_health.py`, `lib/generate_codemap.py`, `lib/summarize_session.py`\n- (batch-read in full by Explore agents) all 70 `hooks/*.sh|*.py` + all 14 `lib/*` files\n\nkb surfacing system (`~/Projects/ai/kb`):\n- (batch-read in full) all 15 `kb/hooks/*.py` incl. `_seen.py`, `_state.py`, `_canonical_match_cli.py`; `scripts/hooks/*`\n- diffed `lean_py_surface.py` vs `py_lean_surface.py` (NOT duplicates — complementary directions)\n\nPhysics persona system (`~/Physics`):\n- `secular-constraints/.claude/settings.json`, `hooks/session-persona.sh`, `hooks/typing-checklist-reminder.sh`\n- `secular-constraints/.claude/agents/personas/tip.md` (+ Explore-read archie/carl/emmy/pip), `agents/verification-orchestrator.md`, `commands/persona.md`, `commands/verify-orchestrate.md`, `rules/physics-antipatterns.md`\n- `claude/.claude/settings.json`, `claude/.claude/hooks/session-persona.sh` (stale copy)\n\nBd: kb-7mk, kb-6hn read in full (cross-refs, NOT absorbed).\n\n## Goal\n\nThe GLOBAL `~/.claude` config must have **zero reference to `~/Physics`** or to physics/lean/tex/cl44/persona content. Topic-specific hooks live in the respective repos' `.claude/settings.json`. The generic kb-surfacing machinery and the persona *mechanism* move into `~/.claude`; the persona *bodies* stay in `~/Physics/secular-constraints`.\n\n## Verified findings (triage)\n\n### Coupling to remove from GLOBAL settings.json\nPhysics hook *files* in `~/.claude/hooks/` to MOVE to `secular-constraints/.claude/hooks/`:\n`annotate-traces.sh`, `block-approximations.sh`, `block-scratch-imports.sh`, `prior-art-gate.sh`, `quarantine-paths.sh`, `archie-report-ingest.sh`, `bd-inprogress-stop.sh`, `tip-stop-lean-queue.sh`.\nkb/py physics hooks (already in kb repo, just de-wire from global): `lean_py_surface`, `py_lean_surface`, `lake_error_surface`, `lean_write_guard`, `bd_close_reingest`, `python_tex_backref`, `tex_section_context`, `tex_stale_surface`, `check_symbols`.\n\n### Per-repo Physics state (asymmetric)\n- **secular-constraints**: canonical + richest config — already wires all physics/lean/tex hooks + `typing-checklist-reminder.sh` + Stop hooks + `session-persona.sh`. NOTE: it references two hooks via `$HOME/Projects/ai/claude/hooks/...` (= `~/.claude`) — fix to local path after the files move.\n- **claude**: stale *subset* of secular's settings; stale `session-persona.sh`.\n- **mathlib4**: NO `.claude/` — must gain a minimal `settings.json` wiring the lean hooks it relies on (lost when global is stripped).\n\n### Persona mechanism\nCanonical = secular's `session-persona.sh` (newer: session-id pin, cwd-safety, RESUME PROTOCOL injection). Only physics bits: hardcoded `$HOME/Physics/...personas` fallback + the agent-id→persona case-map. Personas carry `role:` frontmatter (tip.md: `role: tip`) → generic resolver reads `role:` instead of the case-map.\n\n### Generic kb-surfacing (MOVE into ~/.claude/hooks per user decision)\n`_seen.py`, `_state.py`, `_canonical_match_cli.py`, `open_issues_surface.py`, `symbol_surface.py`, `compose_time_check.py` core. Dependency: physics kb/hooks staying in the kb repo import `_seen`/`_state` → after the move they must import from `~/.claude/hooks/lib` (resolve via a stable `sys.path` insert or a symlink kept in the kb repo).\n\n### Anomalies (surfaced)\n- **guard-destructive-git.sh is NOT wired globally** though CLAUDE.md claims enforcement — its bypass-arm `git-asked-gate.sh` IS wired. Wire the guard. (Safety-critical.)\n- **precompact-save-state.sh writes `handoff.md`**, contradicting CLAUDE.md \"state lives in beads; no handoff.md\". Resolve.\n\n### Read-verified dead files (delete) — consumers confirmed absent across hooks/, bin/, commands/, kb/hooks/\n- `build-status.sh`, `history-isolation.sh` — absorbed verbatim into `session-init.sh` (which declares the merge).\n- `dedupe-file-reads.sh` — never wired; abandoned (redundant with read-coverage-gate + dedupe-kb-get).\n- `lib/beads-plan.sh` — only the 4 `plan-*.deprecated` hooks used it; dies with the retired plan-approval stack.\n- `lib/summarize_session.py` — zero consumers; superseded by kb-precompact.sh + extract_session_state/gather_session_context.\n\n### Read-verified LIVE (do NOT delete — rescued from initial scan)\n- `lib/provider-context.sh` — sourced by `bin/claude-statusline`.\n- `lib/ash_health.py` — imported by `kb/hooks/compose_time_check.py` (the `.sh` sibling serves shell hooks).\n- `lib/generate_codemap.py` — backs the `/codemap` command.\n\n### Deprecated/backup/test (delete or relocate)\nDelete: `detect-plan-implementation.sh.deprecated`, `expert-review-reminder.sh.deprecated`, `plan-cleanup.sh.deprecated`, `plan-mode-approved.sh.deprecated`, `plan-write-review.sh.deprecated`, `md-asked-gate.sh.bak`.\nRelocate to `tools/`: `hooks-selftest.sh`, `test-block-text-search.sh`.\n\n### Unwired generics — wire-or-delete decision\nWire: `guard-destructive-git.sh`, `git-commit-check.sh`, `lsp-diagnostics.sh`, `lsp-setup.sh`, `auto-resume.sh`. Delete: `kb-search-gate.sh` (superseded by prior-art-gate's embedding-down gate).\n\n## Phases\n\n- **P0 — verify (DONE, no edits).** Confirmed: session-init absorbed build-status+history-isolation (comment-only refs elsewhere); 5 dead vs 3 live-rescued; claude settings subset of secular settings; lean_py/py_lean are complementary not duplicate.\n- **P1 — safety (independent, first).** Wire `guard-destructive-git.sh` + `git-commit-check.sh` into global PreToolUse/Bash. Resolve `precompact-save-state.sh` handoff.md vs beads (drop handoff.md write or rename to a beads-checkpoint).\n- **P2 — decouple global.** Remove physics/lean/tex hook entries from global `settings.json`; `git mv` the 8 physics hook files to `secular-constraints/.claude/hooks/`; fix secular's two `$HOME/Projects/ai/claude/hooks/...` refs to local paths.\n- **P3 — fill gaps + dedupe.** Create `mathlib4/.claude/settings.json` (lean hooks: lean_write_guard, lake_error_surface, symbol_surface, compose_time_check). Align `claude/.claude/settings.json` to secular's superset. Delete claude's stale `session-persona.sh` (inherits generalized global one).\n- **P4 — infra-parametrize (env not host).** Env-drive `ash`/`tardis`/`models.yaml` in `kb-context`, `kb-precompact`, `kb-flush-pending`, `model-availability`, `project-scaffold-check`, `lib/ash_health.{sh,py}` via `KB_EMBEDDING_URL`/`KB_LLM_URL` (already the kb project convention).\n- **P5 — de-physics mixed-in-place hooks.** Conditional/config branches in `bridge-resume` (persona→handle map), `bridge-recv-prompt` (archie branch), `block-text-search-on-source` (lean/loogle branch — keep generic core), `session-start-resume` (persona name list).\n- **P6 — generalize surfacing + move.** Move `_seen.py`,`_state.py`,`_canonical_match_cli.py`,`open_issues_surface.py`,`symbol_surface.py` + `compose_time_check.py` core into `~/.claude/hooks/`; resolve the kb-repo import path for `_seen`/`_state`; make `symbol_surface`/`open_issues_surface`/`compose_time_check` project-map + table-registry driven (no inlined Physics→algebraic-genesis map).\n- **P7 — persona port.** Generalize secular's `session-persona.sh` (read `role:` frontmatter; `~/.claude/agents/personas` fallback; drop hardcoded Physics path + case-map) → `~/.claude/hooks/`. Port `/persona` → `~/.claude/commands/`. Create `~/.claude/agents/personas/`. Document the persona protocol in `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`.\n- **P8 — cleanup (delete set = 13).** Delete the 5 verified-dead + 6 deprecated/backup; relocate the 2 test harnesses to `tools/`. Delete `kb-search-gate.sh`.\n- **P9 — easy mechanical wins (folded in).** (a) Consolidate the duplicated markdown allowlist: extract shared `lib/md_policy.sh`, have `block-markdown-files.sh` (Write) + `block-markdown-via-bash.sh` (Bash) both source it — removes the two-place drift. (b) Move test harnesses to `tools/` (with P8). Larger reorg → kb-876; boilerplate lib → kb-d81; SessionStart consolidation → kb-6jp.\n\n## Follow-ups (in bd)\n\n- kb-876: Reorganize ~/.claude/hooks into domain subdirs + migrate settings.json paths — out of scope here (cross-repo path churn, needs own migration).\n- kb-h3b: Unify shell session-state dedup onto a shared helper mirroring _seen.py/_state.py — behavior-sensitive, follow-up.\n- kb-d81: Add lib/hook_json.sh stdin-field helper; adopt incrementally — removes per-hook jq boilerplate, follow-up.\n- kb-6jp: Consolidate the 11 SessionStart hooks; audit/normalize timeouts — ordering-sensitive, follow-up.\n- kb-pfc: Generalize verify-orchestrate scaffold (G1/G2/G3 + C0-C4) into ~/.claude/commands — follow-up.\n- kb-9q9: Fix malformed frontmatter in secular verification-orchestrator.md — follow-up.\n\n## Cross-references (not absorbed)\n\n- kb-7mk: check_symbols/H1 global variant — adjacent to P6 genericization; coordinate but separate.\n- kb-6hn: hooks-over-instructions cadence (CLAUDE.md prose -\u003e certified_data/hooks) — distinct in-flight effort; P5/P7 should avoid conflicting edits to compose_time_check/check_symbols wiring.\n\n## Notation\n\n- \"global\" = `~/.claude` = `~/Projects/ai/claude` (single physical dir).\n- \"per-repo physics settings\" = each `~/Physics/\u003crepo\u003e/.claude/settings.json`.\n- \"surfacing\" = hook-injected context (open beads, prior art, reimplementations, symbols).\n","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T14:36:40Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T10:03:15Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T17:48:41Z","close_reason":"All 9 phases done. Global ~/.claude de-physics'd + persona ported global; generic surfacing moved into ~/.claude; safety guard wired; cleanup done. 7 discovered-from follow-ups remain open (skills move, settings access-grants, block-text-search msg, subdir reorg, dedup unify, hook_json, SessionStart consolidation, verify-orchestrate scaffold, frontmatter fix).","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-zma","title":"kb-dev: EMBEDDING-DOWN detection hook — announce degradation + FTS fallback + optional hard-STOP gate","description":"User-ordered (2026-06-07, after the silent-blind re-derivation failure). ash:8081 down = kb-search + [STRUCTURAL-FACT]/[ALREADY-CODIFIED]/[NOTATION] surfacing go SILENT; agents forge ahead blind and re-derive. SIGNAL (cheap): curl -s -m2 -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://ash:8081/ != 200 (4ms when up); also kb 503 / 'Queued:' (add fell to pending). IMPLEMENT: (1) ANNOUNCE — a SessionStart + PreToolUse-on-compute-intent check that, when ash unreachable, injects a LOUD '[EMBEDDING DOWN: kb-search/surfacing BLIND — STOP retrieval-dependent compute, mechanical-only]' line (cache health w/ short TTL, e.g. 60s, to avoid per-call latency); (2) FALLBACK — the surfacing hooks (structural_facts, findings_fts, notations) are sqlite-FTS/exact-match indexed and do NOT need embeddings: make them fall back to FTS when embeddings are down so they STILL fire (degraded but not blind); (3) optional hard-STOP gate per the global CLAUDE.md 'EMBEDDING-SERVER-DOWN HARD STOP' section. Cross-ref: global ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md KB section, kb meta-failure kb-20260607-192654-3ad69e.","notes":"SLOW-degrade landed (this session): added per-call embed timeout; HybridSearch query embed uses KB_SEARCH_EMBED_TIMEOUT (10s) so a SLOW-but-responding server degrades to FTS in seconds (was up to 180s). kb-context.sh SessionStart search bounded (8s embed, 0 retries, timeout 12 outer). Per-prompt surfacing (kb-prompt-surface.py) already had an 8s subprocess cap (skip on slow/down). Plus earlier: FTS fallback on failure, ash_health.sh probes router /health (not /), kb-context SessionStart announce -\u003e stdout. kb-zma CORE COMPLETE: parts (1)announce (2)FTS-fallback (3)hard-STOP all done. ONLY residual = pure-mechanical-edit carve-out for prior-art-gate (obviated now that search is runnable-degraded; lower priority, could spin to its own issue).","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-07T23:31:12Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T12:26:03Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-9n6","title":"kb-dev: lean_work_queue Stop-hook iteration (dogfood bugs #4532) + startup token diet (bd-prime trim, mathlib-contributions generation, proofs_suspicious fold)","description":"A. lean_work_queue (tip's proactive-proving Stop hook, #4518-\u003e#4523 accepted full): fix the dogfood bugs tip filed #4532 — (1) queue-defer subcommand does not exist in kb.py (defer menu unexecutable); (2) row-id display; (3) READINESS-INFERENCE (default DESIGN-NEEDED + the -- CONTRACT-READY: marker); (4) agent-cap awareness; (5) session defer-cache; (6) lake-check --include-working-tree (worktree can't see untracked — bounds new-file concurrency); (7) gap-claim citation mandate + rot lint (#4558/#4559); PLAN-DIVERGENCE auto-flag on old-bead rows (#4527). B. startup token diet (secular-constraints bd onr0): bd-prime SessionStart output ~31K tok EVERY session -\u003e counts+top-N; mathlib-contributions.md 62K -\u003e git-log-generated index; proofs_suspicious.md 26K -\u003e fold into lean-audit/suspect surface. Principle: every cut names where content went. Cross-ref: secular-constraints onr0, bridge #4561/#4523/#4532.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-07T21:53:02Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-07T21:53:02Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-6hn","title":"kb-dev: hooks-over-instructions cadence steps 2-7 (FRAME_PROVENANCE wiring + the CLAUDE.md removal classes)","description":"User doctrine: hooks \u003e sweeping instructions; narrowly-scoped surfacing at need-time. Negotiation #4565-\u003e#4566 (8 YES/1 PARTIAL/1 SPLIT). DONE: step1 sigma* pointer (049a5f8), step4 GK symlink (archie). REMAINING (per-class, content moves to certified_data FIRST then archie cuts CLAUDE.md prose only after observed firing): step2 FRAME_PROVENANCE -\u003e wire python_symbols.frame_hint surfacing into compose_time_check + check_symbols (emmy landed the dict 28f6ba3 + facts.py 98bff02 — DATA READY, just the ~40-line hook wiring left); step3 object glossary (M_HF/tau2/M_vierbein/dilaton_*) -\u003e notations rows (archie supplies dict); step5 mass/gram route-retired -\u003e python_symbols RETIRED rows (R_chi/S_had/detPhiNative + kb-ids); step6 anti-pattern table SPLIT (file-content-\u003eEdit/Write lint; prose-\u003eStop hook ~8 phrases; semantic-\u003estays); step7 personas Stop-surface rule files. Full per-class assessment: secular-constraints bd onr0 + bridge #4566.","notes":"step6 DONE (anti-pattern table SPLIT -\u003e hooks): FILE-CONTENT = new hooks/guards/block-box-drawing.py (PreToolUse Edit|Write, blocks U+2500-U+257F box-drawing in authored content; excludes block-elements/statusline bar). OUTPUT = block-unprompted-deferral.sh BOX category (box-drawing in assistant response text). PROSE rows already enforced by that Stop hook's READ/PAUSE/BRAG (speculation hedges, 'want me to look', 'probably already covers', self-praise). STAY SEMANTIC (too FP-prone or judgment): 'promising/straightforward/just needs', conflict-averaging, label-match, intent-free-test, DFR, grep-blind-audit, out-of-scope-model, epic-without-review, notation-conflict, CLAUDE.md-wins. Suite 53/53; settings PreToolUse[Write|Edit] wired; verifier 63. Per doctrine, the CLAUDE.md box-drawing prose row is cut only AFTER observed firing. REMAINING kb-6hn: step2 (FRAME_PROVENANCE wiring, data ready), step3/5 (notations/RETIRED rows, need archie dicts), step7 (persona Stop-surface).","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-07T21:52:46Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T17:29:51Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-6d3.1","title":"Phase 1: Incremental lean ingest + lean/tex git hooks","description":"Add --files arg to scripts/ingest_lean_direct.py; wire through kb.py ingest lean handler; add lean+tex kb ingest stanzas to ~/Physics/claude/.git/hooks/post-commit; add lean stanza to ~/Physics/mathlib4/.git/hooks/post-commit.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-06T23:56:10Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T10:03:15Z","closed_at":"2026-06-06T23:59:59Z","close_reason":"--files added to ingest_lean_direct.py + kb.py; post-commit hooks extended in claude and mathlib4 repos","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-6d3.1","depends_on_id":"kb-6d3","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-06T19:56:10Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":2,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-6d3","title":"KB Ingest: git hooks, python_symbols, tex_annotations, realtime hooks","description":"Implement PLAN-kb-ingest-hooks.md. Build index of Python symbols + TeX annotation cross-references to prevent agent re-implementation. Five phases: (1) incremental lean ingest + git hooks, (2) lean_theorems↔findings reconciliation, (3) python_symbols table + ingest, (4) tex_annotations table + ingest, (5) real-time H1/H2/H3/A1 Claude Code hooks.","design":"~/.claude/plans/PLAN-kb-ingest-hooks.md","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-06T23:55:55Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T10:03:15Z","closed_at":"2026-06-07T00:19:19Z","close_reason":"all steps complete","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-xoq","title":"Concept Register \u0026 Theorem Index","description":"Add concepts and lean_theorems tables to KB with pointer tables. Concept register provides structured recall layer for thinking-block prefill. Theorem index stores ~1500 Lean declarations from ~/Physics/claude/proofs/ with pure-math restatements. Enables narrowing pipeline: question → concept match → theorem pointer → thinking prefill.","design":"# Plan: Concept Register \u0026 Theorem Index for KB\n\n## Objective\n\nAdd two new entity types to the knowledge base — **concepts** and **lean\ntheorems** — with pointer tables between them and existing findings. These\nform the structured recall layer that enables thinking-block prefill for\nLLM sessions: inject domain-specific verified knowledge as reasoning\ncontext, then discard it after generation.\n\n## Background \u0026 Motivation\n\nLLMs with long context exhibit a specific memory failure: factual recall of\ndistinctive tokens remains strong, but retrieval of conceptual conclusions\ndegrades. The model can reproduce \"0.204 degrees\" but cannot answer \"what\ndid you conclude about the gauge group?\" Conceptual conclusions compete with\nhundreds of similar passages in the attention softmax.\n\nThe concept register is a persistent, compact buffer of active conclusions\nthat is always visible (prepended to thinking context). Combined with a\ntheorem index, it enables a narrowing pipeline: question → concept match →\ntheorem pointer dereference → inject relevant theorems into thinking block.\n\n**Critical design constraint**: Domain association is net negative for novel\ntheories. The thinking prefill must use pure mathematical language, not\nphysics framing. Telling the model NOT to do something activates the\nassociation. Instead: mention only the correct framework and techniques.\n\nSource: `~/.claude/plans/PLAN-concept-memory.txt` (original spec on tardis)\n\n## Schema Design\n\n### lean_theorems table\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE lean_theorems (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,          -- opaque: \"thm-20260404-123456-abc\"\n    lean_name TEXT NOT NULL,      -- Lean qualified name (for REPL lookup)\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,           -- Short human name\n    statement TEXT NOT NULL,      -- Original statement (source of truth)\n    statement_pure TEXT,          -- Neutral math restatement (for injection)\n    declaration TEXT NOT NULL,    -- Full theorem declaration line(s)\n    module TEXT,                  -- Lean module path (for routing)\n    file TEXT NOT NULL,           -- File path relative to proof root\n    line INTEGER,\n    tex_source TEXT,              -- Cross-ref: \"LAGRANGIAN.tex line 47\"\n    project TEXT,\n    tags TEXT,                    -- JSON array\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n```\n\nKey decisions:\n- ID is opaque (no domain activation from Lean module names in IDs)\n- `lean_name` stored separately for REPL lookup\n- `statement_pure` is LLM-rewritten at ingestion time — neutral math language\n- `module` is routing metadata only, never rendered into thinking prefill\n\n### concepts table\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE concepts (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    domain TEXT NOT NULL,         -- Routing only, never rendered\n    status TEXT DEFAULT 'open'\n        CHECK(status IN ('open','active','verified','superseded','procedure')),\n    claim TEXT NOT NULL,          -- One-line pure math statement (\u003c30 tokens)\n    correct_framing TEXT,         -- Positive restatement for ambiguous cases\n    supersedes_id TEXT REFERENCES concepts(id),\n    project TEXT,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n```\n\nKey decisions:\n- `correct_framing` replaces `invalidation_guard` — positive only, never negations\n- `procedure` status for HOW-TO rules (basis change protocol, etc.)\n- `claim` is always in pure math language\n- `domain` used for narrowing routing, never appears in thinking prefill\n\n### Pointer tables\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE concept_theorems (\n    concept_id TEXT REFERENCES concepts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    theorem_id TEXT REFERENCES lean_theorems(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    role TEXT DEFAULT 'evidence'\n        CHECK(role IN ('evidence','depends_on','motivates')),\n    PRIMARY KEY (concept_id, theorem_id)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE concept_findings (\n    concept_id TEXT REFERENCES concepts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    finding_id TEXT REFERENCES findings(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    role TEXT DEFAULT 'evidence',\n    PRIMARY KEY (concept_id, finding_id)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE theorem_dependencies (\n    theorem_id TEXT REFERENCES lean_theorems(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    depends_on_id TEXT REFERENCES lean_theorems(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    PRIMARY KEY (theorem_id, depends_on_id)\n);\n```\n\n### Vector tables (added in init_schema)\n\n```sql\nCREATE VIRTUAL TABLE lean_theorems_vec USING vec0(\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, embedding float[{dim}]\n);\nCREATE VIRTUAL TABLE concepts_vec USING vec0(\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, embedding float[{dim}]\n);\n```\n\n## Implementation Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Schema + Repositories (2 days)\n\n1. Add tables to `kb/core/schema.py`\n2. Create `kb/entities/theorems.py` — TheoremRepository\n   - add, get, search(query, module, project), search_by_tex_source\n   - list_module(path), add_dependency, get_dependencies\n   - Embedding on `statement_pure` (fallback: `statement`)\n3. Create `kb/entities/concepts.py` — ConceptRepository\n   - add, get, verify, supersede, link_theorem, link_finding\n   - list(domain, status, project), get_theorems, get_findings\n   - render_register(project, max_tokens)\n4. Wire into facade.py\n\n### Phase 2: MCP Tools (1 day)\n\nCore tools (kb_mcp_core.py — always available):\n- `theorem_search(query, module, project)` — semantic + FTS search\n- `concept_add(domain, claim, status, correct_framing, project)`\n- `concept_get(id)` — full concept with linked theorems + findings\n- `concept_render_register(project, max_tokens)` — compact thinking prefill\n\nAdvanced tools (kb_mcp_advanced.py):\n- `theorem_add(lean_name, statement, declaration, file, ...)`\n- `theorem_get(id)`, `theorem_list_module(path)`\n- `concept_verify(id)`, `concept_supersede(id, new_claim, reason)`\n- `concept_link_theorem(concept_id, theorem_id, role)`\n- `concept_link_finding(concept_id, finding_id, role)`\n\n### Phase 3: Lean Ingestion Script (2 days)\n\n`scripts/ingest_lean.py`:\n1. Walk `~/Physics/claude/proofs/` directory\n2. Parse `.lean` files for top-level theorem/lemma declarations\n3. Filter: skip helper lemmas (heuristic: only top-level, in files with\n   MATHEMATICAL OVERVIEW header comments)\n4. Extract: name, statement (the `: Type` part), full declaration,\n   file path, line number, module (from directory structure)\n5. For each theorem: call local LLM to generate `statement_pure`\n   (neutral math restatement)\n6. Store via `theorem_add`\n7. Parse `-- source: FILE.tex line N` comments for tex_source cross-refs\n\nScale: ~9700 .lean files, ~166k declarations total. After filtering to\nmeaningful top-level theorems: estimate ~2000-5000. LLM rewrite at ingestion\nadds ~1 second per theorem = ~1 hour for initial ingestion.\n\n### Phase 4: Register Renderer (1 day)\n\nThe `render_register` method is the critical output interface. It produces\na compact text block for injection into the thinking block.\n\nFormat:\n```\n[FRAMEWORK: graded algebra, exterior calculus, representation theory]\n[TECHNIQUE: basis change via conjugation, direct algebraic manipulation]\n\nVERIFIED:\n- basis_count: exterior algebra on 4-generator module has 2⁴=16 basis elements [thm-001]\n- anomaly_cancel: traceless diagonal operator on Λ*(V) has Tr(Q^(2k+1))=0 [thm-042]\n\nACTIVE:\n- color_classification: diagonal subalgebra commuting with SU(2) generators (partial)\n\nPROCEDURES:\n- basis_change: to express X in basis B', compute B'⁻¹·X·B\n```\n\nBudget: ~30 tokens per concept × 20 concepts = 600 tokens.\n\nThe header lines (FRAMEWORK, TECHNIQUE) are configurable per project.\nThey prime the correct reasoning patterns without mentioning what to avoid.\n\n### Phase 5: Concept Bootstrap (2 days)\n\nSemi-automated population of the initial concept register:\n1. Cluster theorem declarations by file/topic\n2. For each cluster, LLM proposes a concept summary (claim in pure math)\n3. Human reviews and edits\n4. Link theorems to concepts via concept_link_theorem\n5. Identify cross-cutting concepts (basis independence, tracelessness, etc.)\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n1. `theorem_search(\"exterior algebra basis count\")` returns the correct theorem\n2. `concept_render_register(\"exterior_algebra\")` produces \u003c600 token output\n3. For a concept with 3 linked theorems, `concept_get` returns all 3\n4. Lean ingestion processes ~/Physics/claude/proofs/ without errors\n5. `statement_pure` fields use no physics-specific terminology\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Embedding server (ash:8080) for vector search\n- Local LLM (tardis) for statement_pure generation at ingestion time\n- Lean files at ~/Physics/claude/proofs/\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- Lean REPL integration (that's llamacpp-8v9)\n- Thinking block dump mechanism (that's llamacpp-8v9 Phase 0)\n- Experiment harness for comparing thinking prefill vs. context (that's exterior_algebra epic)\n","notes":"SIMPLEMEM INSIGHTS (2026-04-04, from Omni-SimpleMem arXiv:2604.01007):\n\nThree additions to the plan, informed by SimpleMem's autoresearch-validated architecture:\n\n1. SELECTIVE INGESTION WITH NOVELTY FILTER\nBefore theorem_add, check embedding similarity against existing entries. If \u003e0.95 cosine to an existing theorem, flag as potential duplicate and prompt for review. Prevents the ingestion script from adding redundant entries (e.g. helper lemmas that restate a main theorem). Add to TheoremRepository.add() as a pre-check.\n\n2. TOKEN-BUDGET-AWARE RETRIEVAL IN render_register\nThe render_register method should do greedy expansion by similarity-per-token ratio:\n- Score each concept by query_similarity / token_cost_of_its_theorems\n- Add concepts in descending score order until max_tokens budget exhausted\n- This prefers concepts with short, highly-relevant theorems over long, moderately-relevant ones\nSimpleMem calls this 'pyramid expansion' — we do it at the concept→theorem level.\n\n3. DISTANCE-DECAYED GRAPH EXPANSION FOR theorem_dependencies\nWhen retrieving theorems via dependency traversal, weight by hop distance:\n  relevance = beta^d * base_relevance  (beta=0.5, d=hop count)\nDirect dependencies are more relevant than transitive ones. Add distance parameter to get_dependencies(theorem_id, max_hops=3, decay=0.5).\n\nALSO VALIDATED BY SIMPLEMEM:\n- Our MAU≈theorem entry structure independently converged (summary+embedding+pointer+links)\n- Hybrid dense+sparse+graph search matches our embedding+FTS5+pointer approach\n- Set-union merging outperforms score-based fusion — use union for concept register + embedding results\n- Simplicity wins: 15-25 concepts at ~30 tokens each is the right scale\n- Bug fixes \u003e architecture \u003e hyperparameters — focus on correct theorem coverage, not retrieval algorithms\n- Our supersession chain (supersedes_id) is MORE rigorous than SimpleMem (they don't handle corrections)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-04-04T11:37:57Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-04-05T01:49:00Z","closed_at":"2026-04-04T13:31:58Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
