{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-94j","title":"Restore 'deferred' trigger in block-followup-without-bd-id.sh + add regression test","description":"TEMPORARY exemption taken 2026-06-09: the 'deferred?(\\s+to)?' trigger in ~/.claude/hooks/block-followup-without-bd-id.sh was commented out to let PLAN-persistent-session-state.md (whose subject is the 'owed-deferred' file) be written. RESTORE the trigger verbatim once that plan (kb-h3b) is expert-reviewed. While restoring, add a run_hook_tests.py regression case proving (a) 'deferred to follow-up epic' without bd-ID still BLOCKS, and (b) a line mentioning the literal 'owed-deferred' filename does NOT block. Consider the precision fix (require 'deferred to') as the permanent form instead of bare 'deferred'.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-09T21:48:30Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-09T23:25:11Z","closed_at":"2026-06-09T23:25:11Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-94j","depends_on_id":"kb-h3b","type":"discovered-from","created_at":"2026-06-09T17:51:01Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.14","title":"bridge-thread -\u003e kb ingest (vector-searchable team memory); experiential = curation+surfacing, not a new type","description":"Reframe (per maintainer): the kb ALREADY IS the shared multi-agent memory (vector-searchable, cross-agent). 'Code as Agent Harness' (2605.18747 §3.2) distinguishes experiential vs semantic memory, but in OUR stack that collapses into the kb 'type' field — an experiential 'lesson' is just a failure/correction/success finding whose content is 'tried X -\u003e failed (Y) -\u003e fix Z' rather than a static fact. The CLAUDE.md Anti-Patterns table is the hand-promoted subset; kb-mrl reinvention-guard is the deterministic surface. So NO new memory subsystem + NO new 'experience' type. The ONE net-new capability: ingest the bridge (~/.agent-bridge/messages.jsonl) into the kb so resolved threads (--needs-reply resolutions, CLEAR/findings, design negotiations) become vector-searchable team memory instead of evaporating. Scope: (1) bridge-\u003ekb ingest — thread-aware (group reply chains via reply_to), dedup, domain/sender tags, skip ephemeral wake/ack/announce noise; (2) surfacing weights failure/correction (experiential) findings at task-start via existing kb-7g9 hooks. Distinct from §5.2.4 shared-STATE (coordination/consistency); this is the LEARNING layer. Depends-on/extends kb-7g9 bd-\u003ekb ingest + kb-mrl.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-09T20:28:09Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-09T20:28:09Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.14","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-09T16:28:08Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.13","title":"Relevant-but-UNEXPLORED surfacing: per-agent explored-set + on-topic code the agent hasn't opened","description":"User requirement: proactively surface code relevant to the agent's CURRENT work that it HASN'T explored yet (not just 'don't reimplement'). Mechanism: EXPLORED-SET per agent = files/symbols Read or Edited this session (derive from session tool history; reuse _seen/dedupe-file-reads infra). WORKING-SET/topic = recent edits + current file + dispatch prompt -\u003e query. SURFACE = top code symbols semantically/containment-relevant to working-set MINUS explored-set, ranked by relevance x unexplored x importance (public API / high fan-in). Especially surface relevant SUBMODULES the agent hasn't imported/opened (audie: model/ found 527x but core/eval/data missed). Triggers: session-start ('relevant areas you have not opened') + on-topic during work. Inverse of dedup: dedup suppresses seen; this actively surfaces relevant-UNSEEN.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T22:50:10Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T22:50:10Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.13","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T18:50:09Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.11","title":"P0 reliability: JSONL degraded-read fallback when dolt down (bd dark, not read-only)","description":"During the outage bd was TOTALLY DARK (no-db/JSONL mode off, no issues.jsonl export present) — even reads failed. Enable a periodic issues.jsonl export so a server outage is read-only-degraded, not dark. Data itself was safe (dolt dir + backup/).","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:59:47Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T23:16:07Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T23:16:07Z","close_reason":"JSONL export snapshot (.beads/issues.jsonl, 58 issues) + events-export=true + backup.enabled=true (auto periodic export to git remote). Data now always exportable/recoverable + a no-db degraded READ source exists. True AUTO-fallback (bd reading JSONL when dolt down) is bd no-db-mode/upstream — achievable part done.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.11","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:59:46Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.12","title":"P0 reliability: supervise ash:8081 embedding server + embedding-down STOP (pairs kb-zma)","description":"ash:8081 (embeddings) is the same failure class as the dolt server: unsupervised shared backend whose death silently disables a core capability (semantic surfacing goes blind). Supervise (systemd Restart=always) + the embedding-down STOP/FTS-fallback gate (kb-zma) so surfacing hard-STOPs rather than returning silent-empty. Surfacing Tier B + kb surface depend on this.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:59:47Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T21:59:47Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.12","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:59:46Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.8","title":"Provenance-guard trigger: code introduced by patch/commit X — revert, don't layer","description":"mes #5094 (0069-\u003e0071 patch-of-a-patch, reverted). At PreToolUse Edit/Write attribute edited lines/symbol to introducing commit/patch (git-blame vs base, or scan patch-stack 0NNN-*.patch unified-diff hunks) -\u003e WARN revert-not-layer. Rides Tier-A git-provenance. Embedding-free. Specialization: linux-p2p 0NNN-*.patch. #4 same-field-many-patches=cross-patch dup signal. mes offered to co-define the attribution scan.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:42:42Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T21:42:42Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.8","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:42:41Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.4","title":"Tier B: function/block embeddings + current vs history corpora (ash-gated)","description":"Embed qualname:signature:docstring (+ block-level for migrated subspans) for semantic 'different code same intent'. Current tier (working tree, mutable, pruned to HEAD/branch) + History tier (deleted/reverted/branch-tip versions, content-deduped, provenance-tagged). Gated on ash:8081 + the embedding-down STOP (kb-zma). LIVE-TEST on ash return: code-model capability, similarity/threshold calibration, containment vs cosine behavior.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:17:07Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T21:17:07Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.4","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:17:06Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.5","title":"bd-\u003ekb ingest: bd_issues table + _vec, synced on bd create/update/close","description":"Embed bd title+description+design into a bd_issues corpus (+_vec) so kb surface --sources findings,bd,code covers open issues. Sync hook on bd create/update/close (pattern: bd_close_reingest.py) + periodic full resync. Answers your explicit Q: yes, bd must be embedded to vector-search it.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:17:07Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-11T09:50:16Z","closed_at":"2026-06-11T09:50:16Z","close_reason":"Superseded by epic kb-sg0 (bd-\u003ekb full replacement): the ingest-MIRROR approach (bd_issues table synced from dolt) duplicated content; kb-sg0 makes kb the SOURCE OF TRUTH for issues instead. Surfacing work folds into kb-sg0.5.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.5","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:17:06Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7g9.6","title":"Surfacing: kb surface multi-source CLI + function-first/LSP-composing format + layered Edit/Write triggers","description":"kb surface '\u003ctext\u003e' --sources findings,bd,code --limit 3 (embed once, query findings_vec+bd_vec+code tiers, merge by sim/containment). Hook on UserPromptSubmit+PreToolUse(Edit|Write|Task)+Stop. Function-first output (qualname+sig+docstring; file:line metadata for LSP jump). Layered triggers: (1) WRONG-\u003eRIGHT anti-pattern docs in persona, (2) project reinvention-guard pattern-\u003esymbol map, (3) semantic+containment surface. _seen dedup (code:\u003csymbol_id\u003e), suppress-surface allowlist, embedding-down gate.","notes":"AGENT FEEDBACK: Edit/Write ranking UNANIMOUS (a)existing FUNCTION \u003e\u003e (b)reverted/provenance (very-high sim only) \u003e (c)bd PLAN (file in scope) \u003e (d)kb finding. FORMAT: name(sig)-\u003eRet [file:line], one line, function-first, never file-only. COUNT tiered: Bash top-1 high-bar-or-silent; Edit/Write/Stop top-3. Strict per-session dedup load-bearing. SUPPRESS non-code bash + READ + self-match. Past-experiment surfacing at prompt (722-script problem) via kb entries.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T21:17:07Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T22:56:05Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-7g9.6","depends_on_id":"kb-7g9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T17:17:07Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-7lp","title":"UserPromptSubmit: semantic kb query on the incoming prompt (inject matching ids)","description":"audie audit (#5073): UserPromptSubmit runs kb-flush-pending + bridge-recv but never queries kb with the user's message. Prompts like 'prefill order'/'DAG KV cache' get no kb injection though matching entries exist. Fix: UserPromptSubmit step 'kb search \u003cprompt-truncated\u003e --limit 3' -\u003e 1-line 'Relevant KB: ...'; emit nothing if kb down/empty. Pairs with the kb-context.sh semantic fix.","notes":"mes-researcher bridge #5149 feedback (2026-06-09): [OPEN-BD] surfacing WORKED (put exterior_algebra-eqf3/ub49 in PreToolUse context, prevented a dup bd) but agent cited from the TRUNCATED one-line summary and kept doing own analysis; only ran 'bd show' late. Gap: surfaced bead-ID treated as citation token, not 'STOP and retrieve/claim the existing design.' Ask: (a) PreToolUse/Edit hook that BLOCKS Write until a topic-matching surfaced bead is retrieved this session (like followup-bd-id gate); (b) inject the bead's design-file PATH not just truncated title; (c) session-state marker 'N surfaced-but-unretrieved beads relevant to current work.' Real payoff: late retrieval surfaced a load-bearing discrepancy (landed patch 0117 flat slot offset vs ub49 verified gang-indexed offset). Design the retrieve-and-connect enforcement on top of OPEN-BD surfacing.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T20:19:10Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-09T14:04:31Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-k3i","title":"open_issues_surface.py: domain-aware bd injection (single tracker, 2 workstreams — kernel P0/P1 crowd out research)","description":"audie audit (#5073): no SessionStart hook surfaces the main open bd queue; session-followups.sh only catches discovered-from on recently-closed epics. Fresh agents never see 40+ open issues/epics unless they run bd ready. Fix: SessionStart hook 'bd ready --json | head -N' -\u003e compact ids+titles injection. Note overlap: open_issues_surface.py surfaces bd on Task DISPATCH (token-match), not at SessionStart.","notes":"AGENT FEEDBACK #5103-5106 (audie/am-rs-dev/lisa/braidinfer): current [OPEN-BD] is untargeted rotation of open P1s on non-code bash = NOISE; banner-blind after ~3. Missing axis is RELEVANCE-TO-CURRENT-WORK not domain (braidinfer: deep in 50gg.6, never saw 50gg.*). Fixes: gate on CONTENT match to call target not recency/priority; prompt-vocabulary classifier (audie); SUPPRESS pure-IO bash + READ + self/own-active-epic; top-1 high-bar on Bash else silent.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T20:19:10Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T22:56:04Z","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
