{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-bp4.2","title":"P1b: resolve precompact handoff-doc vs beads — NOT a one-line drop (has consumer)","description":"precompact-save-state.sh whole purpose is building the sessions per-id handoff doc; session-start-resume.sh CONSUMES it; it also writes resume TTY pointer files. CLAUDE.md says state-in-beads no handoff doc, BUT this lives in the gitignored session cache, not a project artifact. Multiple valid resolutions (delete+rewrite session-start-resume to bd/kb only; redirect snapshot to kb; or treat session-cache as exempt). Needs a user decision before editing. Discovered during P1.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T15:35:30Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-08T16:00:17Z","closed_at":"2026-06-08T16:00:17Z","close_reason":"handoff.md deprecated per user decision; committed 9c79c11 (~/.claude)","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-bp4.2","depends_on_id":"kb-bp4","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-06-08T11:35:30Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-876","title":"Reorganize ~/.claude/hooks into domain subdirs (bridge/ kb/ guards/ session/ git/) + migrate settings.json paths","description":"Mechanical but cross-repo: ~50 path edits in global settings.json + physics repo settings that reference $HOME/Projects/ai/claude/hooks/*. Must update statusline + physics settings refs atomically. Deferred from kb-bp4 P9 as needing its own careful migration.","design":"# PLAN: Reorganize ~/.claude/hooks into domain subdirs (kb-876)\n\n## Problem / goal\n\n`~/.claude/hooks/` has 55 top-level hook files in one flat directory. Reorganize\ninto domain subdirs (bridge/ git/ kb/ guards/ session/ lsp/ misc/) for\nmaintainability. Pure organization — NO behavior change. lib/ and tests/ stay put.\n\nBlast radius is severe: a hook is wired by absolute path in settings.json, so a\nmissed path = the hook silently STOPS FIRING (a guard disappears with no error).\nTherefore every step is verified by a settings-path checker before commit.\n\n## Inventory (Explore, 2026-06-09) — with one correction\n\n- 55 top-level hook files → 7 domains (table below).\n- 50 hook path refs in the global settings.json (real file\n  `~/Projects/ai/claude/settings.json`; `~/.claude` is a symlink to it).\n  settings.local.json (global) and the secular-constraints / Physics project\n  settings have ZERO `hooks/` path refs — global settings is the only consumer.\n- Test harness `tests/run_hook_tests.py` hardcodes `HOOKS = ~/.claude/hooks` and\n  joins bare filenames → breaks on subdir move; must resolve recursively.\n- `hooks/hooks/` does NOT exist (the earlier `find` listed `hooks` because the\n  scan ran from inside; ignore).\n\nCORRECTION to the inventory's \"inter-hook refs\" classification: it marked\n`source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/lib/X\"` as \"SAFE: uses $(dirname \"$0\")\". That is WRONG.\n`$(dirname \"$0\")` is the script's OWN dir; after moving `foo.sh` →\n`session/foo.sh`, `$(dirname \"$0\")/lib` resolves to `session/lib` (absent). So\nALL of these break on move and must be repointed:\n  - `$(dirname \"$0\")/lib/...` (shell): bd-lifecycle, dedupe-kb-get,\n    incompleteness-gate, incompleteness-scanner, kb-precompact, kb-search-track,\n    precompact-save-state, session-followups, session-init, session-precheck,\n    session-start-resume.\n  - python `os.path.dirname(__file__)+/lib` or `~/.claude/hooks/lib`:\n    bridge-owed-reply-stop, compose_time_check, kb-prompt-surface,\n    open_issues_surface (4).\n  - hardcoded `$HOME/.claude/hooks/lib/X` shell exec wrappers: read-coverage-gate,\n    read-dep-augment, redirect-tmp-scripts, block-markdown-files,\n    block-markdown-via-bash (5).\n  - sibling-hook ref: block-text-search-on-source → `_grep_pipeline_analyzer.py`\n    (moves WITH it into guards/, so this ref becomes intra-guards).\n  - `lib/get_terminal_id.sh` is referenced via `$CLAUDE_DIR/hooks/lib/` (absolute)\n    in precompact-save-state — already move-safe.\nNOTE: hooks IN lib/ that import siblings via `os.path.dirname(__file__)` (e.g.\nread_coverage_gate.py importing _state) are SAFE — lib/ does not move.\n\n## Domain categorization (55 files)\n\n- bridge/ (9): bridge-owed-reply-stop.py, bridge-recv-prompt.sh, bridge-resume.sh,\n  bridge-unread-stop.sh, bridge-watcher-alive.sh, bridge-watcher-check.sh,\n  _bridge_watch_detector.py, block-bridge-watch-background.sh,\n  block-stop-without-bridge-watcher.sh\n- git/ (4): bd-lifecycle.sh, git-asked-gate.sh, git-commit-check.sh,\n  guard-destructive-git.sh\n- kb/ (10): compose_time_check.py, dedupe-kb-get.sh, kb-context.sh,\n  kb-error-extract.sh, kb-flush-pending.sh, kb-precompact.sh, kb-prompt-surface.py,\n  kb-search-track.sh, open_issues_surface.py, symbol_surface.py\n- guards/ (16): incompleteness-gate.sh, incompleteness-scanner.sh,\n  weak-claim-gate.sh, block-markdown-files.sh, block-markdown-via-bash.sh,\n  md-asked-gate.sh, md-cleanup.sh, block-local-dolt-server.sh, block-large-heredoc.sh,\n  block-text-search-on-source.sh, _grep_pipeline_analyzer.py, block-print-spam.sh,\n  block-presentation-cells.sh, block-followup-without-bd-id.sh,\n  block-unprompted-deferral.sh, prior-art-gate.sh, read-coverage-gate.sh\n  (note: read-coverage-gate is a guard; 17 items listed — read-coverage-gate.sh\n  counts here, read-dep-augment.sh -\u003e misc as it is advisory not blocking)\n- session/ (7): session-followups.sh, session-init.sh, session-persona.sh,\n  session-precheck.sh, session-start-resume.sh, precompact-save-state.sh,\n  project-scaffold-check.sh\n- lsp/ (3): lsp-diagnostics.sh, lsp-setup.sh, rust-analyzer-prewarm.sh\n- misc/ (5): allow-env-prefix.py, auto-approve-readonly-bash.py,\n  model-availability.sh, read-dep-augment.sh, redirect-tmp-scripts.sh\n\n(Domain assignment is a detail; reviewer may rebalance guards/ vs misc/ for the\npermission hooks allow-env-prefix / auto-approve-readonly.)\n\n## Files read in full (this plan author)\n\n- `session-init.sh`, `session-precheck.sh`, `precompact-save-state.sh`,\n  `kb-search-track.sh`, `dedupe-kb-get.sh`, `prior-art-gate.sh`,\n  `lib/provider-context.sh`, `lib/state.sh`, `lib/_state.py`,\n  `block-followup-without-bd-id.sh`, `tests/run_hook_tests.py` (all during kb-h3b,\n  same session). Remaining files: header-read via the Explore inventory; each will\n  be Read in full at the phase that touches it.\n\n## Strategy: make lib refs move-invariant FIRST, then move\n\n### Phase 0 — Safety net: settings-path verifier\nAdd `~/.claude/hooks/tests/verify_settings_paths.py`: parse the global\nsettings.json, walk every hooks.*[ ].hooks[ ].command, extract the script path\ntoken (handle `python3 X`, `bash X`, env-prefixed, args), and assert each\nresolves to an existing, executable file. Exit nonzero + list any missing. Run it\nafter EVERY phase below. This is the guard against silent hook loss.\n\n### Phase 1 — Absolute-ize all lib/ + helper references (NO file moves yet)\nConvert every `lib/` reference to absolute `$HOME/.claude/hooks/lib/...` (shell)\n/ `os.path.expanduser('~/.claude/hooks/lib')` (python), so they survive any file\nmove. This is the ~20-file set enumerated in the CORRECTION above. After this,\nmoving a hook file changes ONLY its settings.json path (+ test lookup), not its\ninternals. Verify: run_hook_tests.py 37/37 + a smoke of session-init/statusline.\nCommit.\n\n### Phase 2 — Test harness: resolve hooks recursively\nRefactor `run_hook_tests.py` `bash()/py()` to locate a hook by walking\n`~/.claude/hooks/**` (first match by basename), so it keeps working as files move.\nAdd the Phase-0 verifier invocation to the suite. Verify 37/37. Commit.\n\n### Phases 3–9 — Move one domain per phase (git mv), update settings + test\nFor each domain D in {bridge, git, kb, guards, session, lsp, misc}:\n  1. `git mv` each file into `hooks/D/`.\n  2. Update its settings.json path(s): `hooks/\u003cf\u003e` → `hooks/D/\u003cf\u003e`.\n  3. Update any sibling ref that crosses INTO/OUT of D (only\n     block-text-search-on-source ↔ _grep_pipeline_analyzer, both → guards/, so the\n     ref `$HOME/.claude/hooks/_grep_pipeline_analyzer.py` →\n     `$HOME/.claude/hooks/guards/_grep_pipeline_analyzer.py`).\n  4. Run verify_settings_paths.py (every path must resolve) + run_hook_tests.py.\n  5. Commit per domain (so a regression is bisectable to one domain).\nThe post-commit gate (greps `^(hooks/|settings\\.json$)`) re-runs the suite each\ncommit automatically.\n\n### Phase 10 — Final verification\nFull suite + verifier + a live smoke: trigger one hook per domain (e.g. a\nblock-text-search attempt, a session-init run, a bridge recv) and confirm it\nfires. Confirm `git status` clean and settings.json has zero stale `hooks/\u003cf\u003e`\n(non-subdir) paths via the verifier.\n\n## Risks / mitigations\n\n- Silent guard loss → Phase-0 verifier run every phase; per-domain commits keep\n  blast radius to one domain.\n- settings.json hot-reloads mid-migration → each phase leaves settings + files\n  CONSISTENT (move + path-edit in the same commit), so no window where a path is\n  stale. Within a phase, edit settings AFTER git mv so a reload never points at a\n  not-yet-moved file… (reviewer: confirm ordering — see open question).\n- A second live session resuming mid-reorg picks up a half-updated settings.json:\n  each commit is internally consistent, so worst case a session loads between two\n  consistent states. Acceptable; announce on the bridge before starting.\n- physics-edit-prior-art.sh (secular-constraints) references\n  `$HOME/.claude/hooks/lib/state.sh` (absolute) — unaffected by the move.\n\n## Open question for reviewer\n\nWithin a phase, is \"git mv then edit settings.json\" safe against a hot-reload\nlanding between the two file writes? If the reload reads settings BEFORE the path\nedit, it points at the OLD path (file already moved → missing). Safer ordering may\nbe: stage both, or edit settings to the new path in the same write batch. Reviewer\nto confirm the atomicity story (or accept the ~ms window as negligible for an\norg-only change).\n\n## Follow-ups (in bd)\n\n- (none — kb-876 is self-contained; sequencing dep on kb-h3b is satisfied, kb-h3b closed.)\n","notes":"SEQUENCING: run AFTER kb-h3b (persistent session-state migration). kb-h3b edits the CONTENTS of ~14 state-consumer hooks to repoint /tmp/claude-kb-state -\u003e ~/.claude/state via lib/state.sh; kb-876 MOVES those same files into domain subdirs (bridge/ kb/ guards/). Doing the reorg first would invalidate kb-h3b's source-path references and the inventory. Land kb-h3b, then reorg.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T14:36:59Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T10:03:15Z","closed_at":"2026-06-10T00:21:37Z","close_reason":"all steps complete","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-876","depends_on_id":"kb-bp4","type":"discovered-from","created_at":"2026-06-08T10:36:58Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-h3b","title":"Unify shell session-state dedup onto a shared helper mirroring _seen.py/_state.py","description":"dedupe-kb-get.sh, kb-search-track.sh, (deleted dedupe-file-reads.sh) hand-roll /tmp/claude-kb-state files; python side has _seen.py/_state.py. Build lib/session_seen.sh (or expose the python via CLI) so shell + python share one dedup substrate. Behavior-sensitive -\u003e own task.","design":"# PLAN: Persistent, reboot-surviving session-state root (kb-h3b + folds in \"D\")\n\n## Problem\n\nSession/dedup/defer state lives under `/tmp/claude-kb-state` (tmpfs). A reboot\nwipes it. Concretely observed: `bridge-owed-reply-stop.py`'s deferral log\n(`/tmp/claude-kb-state/owed-deferred`) was lost on the 2026-06-09 reboot, so\nconsciously-deferred owed-replies (within their 6h TTL) re-block as if never\nanswered. The reply *obligations* survive (disk-derived from\n`~/.agent-bridge/messages.jsonl`); only the deferral decisions — and other\nsub-TTL state — are reboot-fragile.\n\nThis is the same consolidation `kb-h3b` already tracks (\"unify shell\nsession-state dedup onto a shared helper mirroring `_seen.py`/`_state.py`\"),\nwith two added requirements: (1) a **persistent root**, (2) **GC** for the file\nclasses that previously relied on `/tmp`'s reboot-wipe. `kb-sdw` (migrate\n`dedupe-*.sh`) is the `dedupe-*.sh` slice of this work.\n\n## Decision (user-approved 2026-06-09)\n\nState root → `~/.claude/state/`. Host-global, reboot-surviving, outside every\ncode repo's tree but inside the (tracked) `~/.claude` git repo — so it MUST be\ngitignored. Filenames keep the existing `\u003csid\u003e-\u003csuffix\u003e` scheme; host-global\nstate (`owed-deferred`, `session-\u003cpid\u003e`) stays un-session-scoped, as today.\n\n## Files read in full\n\n- `~/.claude/hooks/lib/_state.py` — `STATE_DIR='/tmp/claude-kb-state'`; `get_session_id()` (env→PPID walk), `state_path(suffix)`.\n- `~/.claude/hooks/lib/_seen.py` — imports `STATE_DIR, state_path` from `_state`; `\u003csid\u003e-hook-seen`, fcntl-locked.\n- `~/.claude/hooks/session-init.sh` — writes `session-$PPID`; GC: `find -mmin +240 -delete` on `*-searched`, `*-hook-seen`, `session-*`; dead-PID sweep of derived files.\n- `~/.claude/hooks/bridge-owed-reply-stop.py` — `DEFER_FILE='/tmp/claude-kb-state/owed-deferred'`, `DEFER_TTL=6h`; prunes by reading, never trims the file.\n- Blast-radius inventory (Explore, 2026-06-09): 17 hardcoded `/tmp/claude-kb-state` refs across ~14 hooks + 1 physics project hook; 6 centralized via `_state.py`/`_seen.py`.\n\n## Consumer inventory (must all repoint)\n\nCentralized (move with one `_state.py` change): `_seen.py`, `kb-prompt-surface.py`,\n`open_issues_surface.py`, `symbol_surface.py`, `compose_time_check.py`,\n`lib/_canonical_match_cli.py`.\n\nHardcoded shell (`source` the new `lib/state.sh`): `session-init.sh`,\n`session-precheck.sh`, `precompact-save-state.sh`, `incompleteness-scanner.sh`,\n`kb-search-track.sh`, `dedupe-kb-get.sh` (kb-sdw), `prior-art-gate.sh`,\n`lib/provider-context.sh`, `~/Physics/secular-constraints/.claude/hooks/physics-edit-prior-art.sh`.\n\nHardcoded python (use `_state.STATE_DIR`/`state_path`): `bridge-owed-reply-stop.py`,\n`lib/read_coverage_gate.py`, `lib/read_dep_augment.py`.\n\nState file classes: `session-\u003cpid\u003e`, `\u003csid\u003e-searched`, `\u003csid\u003e-hook-seen`,\n`\u003csid\u003e-kb-seen`, `\u003csid\u003e-incomplete-markers`, `\u003csid\u003e-readcov/\u003csha1\u003e` (+ `aug-`),\n`provider-context-window[-\u003cmodel\u003e]`, `owed-deferred`.\n\n## Phases / child tasks (each becomes a bd task under kb-h3b)\n\n1. **Single source of truth.** Add `~/.claude/hooks/lib/state.sh` exporting\n   `STATE_DIR=\"${CLAUDE_STATE_DIR:-$HOME/.claude/state}\"` + `mkdir -p`. Change\n   `_state.py` `STATE_DIR` to `os.environ.get('CLAUDE_STATE_DIR') or\n   os.path.expanduser('~/.claude/state')`. The env override keeps the test\n   harness able to redirect the root (mirrors how `test_wake_filter.sh` uses a\n   throwaway `$HOME`). Add `state/` to `~/.claude/.gitignore`.\n\n2. **Migrate hardcoded shell consumers** to `source lib/state.sh` (drop the\n   literal). Includes `session-init.sh`, `session-precheck.sh`,\n   `precompact-save-state.sh`, `incompleteness-scanner.sh`, `kb-search-track.sh`,\n   `prior-art-gate.sh`, `lib/provider-context.sh`, and the physics project hook.\n\n3. **Migrate `dedupe-*.sh`** (kb-sdw): `dedupe-kb-get.sh` (+ any sibling\n   `dedupe-file-reads.sh` if present) to `lib/state.sh` / `_state.py` lookup.\n   Close kb-sdw on completion.\n\n4. **Migrate hardcoded python consumers**: `bridge-owed-reply-stop.py`\n   (`DEFER_FILE = os.path.join(STATE_DIR, 'owed-deferred')` via `_state`),\n   `read_coverage_gate.py`, `read_dep_augment.py`.\n\n5. **Extend GC** (in `session-init.sh`, runs every SessionStart — already\n   time-based so it works without a reboot-wipe): add `-mmin +240` sweeps for\n   `*-incomplete-markers`, `*-kb-seen`, and `find \u003csid\u003e-readcov -type d -mmin\n   +240 -exec rm -rf`; provider caches by their TTL; and trim `owed-deferred`\n   lines older than `DEFER_TTL` (6h) in place. Goal: bounded growth with no\n   `/tmp` reboot-wipe.\n\n6. **Tests + verify.** Extend `~/.claude/hooks/tests/run_hook_tests.py`:\n   (a) assert `_state.STATE_DIR` resolves under `~/.claude/state` (and honors\n   `CLAUDE_STATE_DIR`); (b) a GC case (seed old files, run the sweep, assert\n   removed); (c) `owed-deferred` persistence: write a defer line, assert\n   `bridge-owed-reply-stop.py` honors it from the persistent path. Run the full\n   suite + `bash -n` all touched shell.\n\n## Migration / cutover\n\nState is ephemeral (dedup/coverage/defer) — **no data migration**. On cutover,\nin-flight sessions' dedup/coverage reset once (re-surface an advisory at most\nonce) and any active deferral is lost once (re-block once, then re-deferrable to\nthe persistent path). One-time cosmetic cost; acceptable. `/tmp/claude-kb-state`\nleft to be reaped naturally; no destructive cleanup.\n\n## Sandbox / permissions\n\n`~/.claude/` is already in the sandbox write-allowlist, so hooks write to\n`~/.claude/state/` without escalation (same as `/tmp/claude-kb-state` today). No\nsettings.json permission change needed.\n\n## Follow-ups (in bd)\n\n- kb-sdw: Migrate `dedupe-kb-get.sh`/`dedupe-file-reads.sh` to `_state.py` lookup — folded in as Phase 3 (dep: discovered-from kb-h3b).\n- kb-94j: Restore the bare-`deferred` trigger in `block-followup-without-bd-id.sh` + add regression test, once this plan is reviewed (a temporary exemption was taken to write this plan).\n","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"epic","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-08T14:36:59Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-10T10:03:15Z","closed_at":"2026-06-09T23:28:52Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"kb-h3b","depends_on_id":"kb-bp4","type":"discovered-from","created_at":"2026-06-08T10:36:59Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","metadata":"{}"}],"dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-w6c","title":"lean_work_queue ingest: auto-classify Mathlib-gap contracts as DESIGN-NEEDED","description":"tip #4532: contracts naming a Mathlib gap are EXECUTE-READY but should be DESIGN-NEEDED. Detect via file_status/proof_grade containing 'absent from Mathlib', 'not in Mathlib', 'Mathlib gap', 'upstream' near a named lemma. Set readiness=DESIGN-NEEDED, defer_reason=design-pending:mathlib-gap.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-07T15:57:57Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-07T15:58:42Z","closed_at":"2026-06-07T15:58:42Z","close_reason":"implemented in ingest_lean_work_queue.py: MATHLIB_GAP_RE detects 'absent from Mathlib' etc., sets DESIGN-NEEDED + auto defer_reason=design-pending:mathlib-gap","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
{"_type":"issue","id":"kb-cqv","title":"lean_contracts: four-axis schema extension (proof_grade, data_blocked_on, operator_version, statement-suspect)","description":"Extend lean_contracts schema with three new columns (tip #4382, emmy #4383, archie #4385 endorsed):\n1. proof_grade TEXT: {sorry-bearing, axiom-bound, native-decide, clean-deep} — derived from lean-audit --json at ingest, NO file annotation needed\n2. data_blocked_on TEXT: nullable bd-id — marks contracts blocked on data landing (gyb.4-blocked pads); WAITING advisories suppress discharge proposals while non-null; trigger re-ingest on bd-close hook\n3. operator_version TEXT: from -- OPERATOR-VERSION: header; staleness check against certified_data\n4. file_status 'statement-suspect' value: ingest promotes lean-audit vacuity-suspect to this (routes to statement REVIEW, not discharge)\n\nMigration: ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN for each new field.\nIngest: parse at ingest time (proof_grade auto-derived, no marker needed).\nHook: compose_time_check advisory updates for data_blocked_on cleared signal.\nbd-close hook: trigger re-ingest when a data_blocked_on bd-id closes (follow-up).","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"Bob McElrath","owner":"mcelrath@users.noreply.github.com","created_at":"2026-06-07T08:25:59Z","created_by":"Bob McElrath","updated_at":"2026-06-07T08:32:57Z","closed_at":"2026-06-07T08:32:57Z","close_reason":"Closed","dependency_count":0,"dependent_count":0,"comment_count":0}
